\begin_body

\begin_layout Chapter
Getting started 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Section
Installation 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Subsection
System requirements
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
A 64-bit operating system: macOS (Apple Silicon), Windows (x86_64) or Linux (x86_64, aarch64).
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
At least 4 GB of memory (8 GB or more are recommended for large images, stacks and volumes).
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
A graphics card with OpenGL for the 3D view (Space view) and the WorldWind view.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
\series bold
R 4.3 or later
\series default
 for the R features of Bio7 (R is not bundled with Bio7, see below).
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
Optional: Python 3.8 or later (embedded Python), Quarto (Quarto documents), pandoc and LaTeX (R Markdown documents and PDF output) and LibreOffice (the LibreOffice features of Bio7). The path to LibreOffice is fetched from the registry (Windows) or can be set in the Bio7 preferences.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Bio7 includes its Java runtime (Eclipse Temurin 27 with Nashorn): no Java installation is needed.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Subsection
Installation
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The installation files of Bio7 are available on the GitHub Releases page of Bio7 (
\begin_inset Flex URL
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
https://github.com/Bio7/bio7/releases
\end_layout

\end_inset

). The checksums of all files are in the file 
\family typewriter
SHA256SUMS.txt
\family default
.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Subsubsection
Windows
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Download the file 
\family typewriter
bio7-<version>-windows-x86_64.zip
\family default
 and unzip it in a folder of your choice (avoid spaces in the path). Start 
\family typewriter
Bio7.exe
\family default
. Bio7 is not signed with a Windows certificate: if SmartScreen warns at the first start, click 
\series bold
More info > Run anyway
\series default
.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Subsubsection
macOS
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Download the file 
\family typewriter
bio7-<version>-macos-aarch64.dmg
\family default
 (Apple Silicon), open it and drag Bio7 to the Applications folder. Bio7 is not notarized by Apple, so macOS blocks it at the first start ("Apple could not verify 'Bio7' is free of malware"). Open 
\series bold
System Settings > Privacy & Security
\series default
, scroll down to the message about Bio7 and click 
\series bold
Open Anyway
\series default
 (once for each version). Alternatively type in the Terminal:
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
\begin_inset listings
lstparams "basicstyle={\ttfamily\small},breaklines=true"
inline false
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
\begin_inset Caption Standard

\begin_layout Plain Layout
Removes the quarantine flag of Bio7 (macOS Terminal)
\end_layout

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Plain Layout
xattr -dr com.apple.quarantine /Applications/Bio7.app
\end_layout

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The camera (e.g., OpenCV in Python) needs the permission of macOS: macOS asks for it the first time. In this case start Bio7 from the Finder or the Dock, not from a terminal.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Subsubsection
Linux
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Download the file 
\family typewriter
bio7-<version>-linux-<arch>.tar.gz
\family default
 (x86_64 or aarch64), unpack it and start 
\family typewriter
Bio7
\family default
. The 3D views (Space view and WorldWind) need the X11 backend of GTK: on a Wayland desktop start Bio7 with 
\family typewriter
GDK_BACKEND=x11 ./Bio7
\family default
 (XWayland).
\end_layout

\begin_layout Subsubsection
The workspace
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
At the first start Bio7 creates its workspace (the default location on macOS is 
\family typewriter
~/Bio7/workspace
\family default
). The projects, the scripts and the settings of Bio7 are stored in the workspace.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Subsection
R in Bio7 (embedded R)
\begin_inset CommandInset label
LatexCommand label
name "subsec:Embedded-R"

\end_inset

\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Bio7 embeds R directly: R runs in the process of Bio7 (with the Foreign Function & Memory API of Java). No Rserve, no JNI and no extra R package is needed: only an installed 
\series bold
R 4.3 or later
\series default
. The data are transferred directly between R and Bio7 (the R-Shell view, the Table view, ImageJ, the editors and the scripts). With an older R version Bio7 reports "Embedded R needs R 4.3 or later".
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Install R from CRAN (
\begin_inset Flex URL
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
https://cran.r-project.org
\end_layout

\end_inset

) with the installer of your operating system (Windows, macOS) or with the package manager (Linux, e.g., 
\family typewriter
sudo apt install r-base
\family default
). Bio7 uses the default installation of R automatically. Another R installation is selected in the R preferences (
\series bold
Preferences Bio7 > Preferences R
\series default
, 
\series bold
Path to R
\series default
). The button 
\series bold
R Setup...
\series default
 (
\series bold
Find or install R
\series default
) searches the installed R versions on this computer: 
\series bold
Use for Bio7
\series default
 sets the path to R (applied at the next start of R). The dialog also helps to install R (the commands for the operating systems, 
\series bold
Open R Download Page
\series default
, on Windows 
\series bold
Install R with winget
\series default
).
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
R is started with 
\series bold
Start R
\series default
 in the main toolbar or in the R menu (optionally at the startup of Bio7: 
\series bold
Preferences Startup
\series default
, 
\series bold
Start R
\series default
; by default R also starts when it is used, e.g., by a script: 
\series bold
Start R when it is used
\series default
). The R preferences describe the restrictions of embedded R:
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
R can be interrupted (
\series bold
Interrupt R
\series default
 in the menu of the Start R action, Ctrl+C in the console or the stop button of the R-Shell view), but not terminated or restarted without a restart of Bio7.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
A crash of R (e.g., of a package) ends Bio7: save your work.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
\family typewriter
parallel::mclapply()
\family default
 runs sequentially (
\family typewriter
mc.cores = 1
\family default
); other parallel methods (e.g., socket clusters) are available.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The memory used by R is displayed in the status line (
\series bold
R: ... MB
\series default
). The R preferences are described in 
\begin_inset CommandInset ref
LatexCommand ref
reference "subsec:Rserve-preferences"
plural "false"
caps "false"
noprefix "false"
nolink "false"

\end_inset

.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
R commands which should run at each start of R (e.g., to set paths) can be added in the field 
\series bold
R startup commands
\series default
 of the R preferences.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Subsection
R packages
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The R packages are installed in the R library of the used R installation (or in the 
\series bold
Package install location
\series default
 of the R preferences) with the Packages view of the R perspective or in R. Some R packages are recommended to use all functions of Bio7 (e.g., for the formatting of R code, R Markdown documents, spatial data and image analysis). They can be installed with a script in the context menu of the R-Shell view (
\series bold
Packages > Install_Default_R_Packages
\series default
).
\end_layout

\begin_layout Subsubsection
R packages Linux specific
\begin_inset CommandInset label
LatexCommand label
name "subsec:R-packages-Linux"

\end_inset

\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
On Linux the R packages are compiled from the sources: the compilers 
\family typewriter
g++
\family default
 and 
\family typewriter
gfortran
\family default
 must be installed. The spatial packages (e.g., sf, terra) need in addition the development files of GDAL, PROJ and GEOS (e.g., 
\family typewriter
libgdal-dev
\family default
, 
\family typewriter
libproj-dev
\family default
, 
\family typewriter
libgeos-dev
\family default
), some packages BLAS and LAPACK (
\family typewriter
libblas-dev
\family default
, 
\family typewriter
liblapack-dev
\family default
).
\end_layout

\begin_layout Subsection
Python in Bio7 (embedded Python)
\begin_inset CommandInset label
LatexCommand label
name "subsec:Embedded-Python"

\end_inset

\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Bio7 embeds Python like R: CPython runs in the process of Bio7 (data transfer with numpy and pandas, matplotlib plots in Bio7, a Python debugger, see 
\begin_inset CommandInset ref
LatexCommand ref
reference "sec:The-Python-Perspective"
plural "false"
caps "false"
noprefix "false"
nolink "false"

\end_inset

). Python is optional and not bundled. 
\series bold
Python 3.8 or later
\series default
 is needed, built with a shared library (e.g., the installers of python.org, Homebrew, conda or the Python of a Linux distribution). The packages numpy, pandas and matplotlib are recommended.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The Python is selected in 
\series bold
Preferences Bio7 > Preferences Python
\series default
:
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
\series bold
Path Python:
\series default
 the folder of the Python installation. 
\series bold
Detect Python...
\series default
 (
\series bold
Find Python on this computer
\series default
) searches the installed Python versions.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
\series bold
Embedded Python:
\series default
 executes the Python code in the process of Bio7 (data transfer, plots). A change of the Python needs a restart of Bio7 (only one Python can run in a Bio7 session).
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
\series bold
Python Packages...
\series default
 (
\series bold
Install, upgrade, uninstall packages
\series default
) opens the Python Packages dialog: it installs, updates and removes packages, installs bundles of packages for Bio7 (scientific, images, OpenCV, editor tools) and can create a virtual environment for Bio7 (
\series bold
Create Bio7 Environment...
\series default
). With 
\series bold
Install packages with uv instead of pip
\series default
 the packages are installed with uv.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
\series bold
Execute Editor Source in Seperate Python Process:
\series default
 executes the scripts of the Python editor in a separate Python process (not in the Python-Shell of Bio7).
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
In the embedded Python 
\family typewriter
exit()
\family default
 and 
\family typewriter
input()
\family default
 are not available.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Subsection
R Markdown and Quarto
\begin_inset CommandInset label
LatexCommand label
name "subsec:RMarkdown-Quarto"

\end_inset

\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
R Markdown documents (*.Rmd) need the R packages rmarkdown and knitr and the program pandoc (
\begin_inset Flex URL
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
https://pandoc.org
\end_layout

\end_inset

). Quarto documents (*.qmd) need Quarto (
\begin_inset Flex URL
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
https://quarto.org
\end_layout

\end_inset

). Bio7 finds pandoc, LaTeX and Quarto also if they are not on the PATH of the system (the default installation folders; Quarto also with the environment variable 
\family typewriter
QUARTO_PATH
\family default
). PDF output needs a LaTeX installation (see below) or, for Quarto, Typst.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
If a program is not found the path can be added to the PATH of R with an R startup command (R preferences, 
\series bold
R startup commands
\series default
), e.g., on macOS:
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
\begin_inset listings
lstparams "basicstyle={\ttfamily\small},breaklines=true"
inline false
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
\begin_inset Caption Standard

\begin_layout Plain Layout
R command to add the paths of pandoc and LaTeX to the PATH of R (macOS)
\end_layout

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Plain Layout
Sys.setenv(PATH = paste(Sys.getenv("PATH"), "/usr/local/bin:/Library/TeX/texbin", sep = ":"))
\end_layout

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The Markdown editor of Bio7 is described in 
\begin_inset CommandInset ref
LatexCommand ref
reference "subsec:The-Markdown-Editor"
plural "false"
caps "false"
noprefix "false"
nolink "false"

\end_inset

.
\end_layout


